WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.028
Hi, I'm Jerry from The Happy Start.

00:00:06.028 --> 00:00:14.640
As a small business owner, one of the most frustrating

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:18.640
feelings is knowing that you have a great product, but it's just sitting there, getting

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:20.287
buried in the search results.

00:00:20.287 --> 00:00:24.240
Today, I want to talk to you about how coupons and promotions

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:25.424
helped us stand out.

00:00:25.424 --> 00:00:28.680
Amazon offers several promotional tools, and one of the most powerful

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:30.954
ones for us is the coupon.

00:00:30.954 --> 00:00:31.712
It's simple.

00:00:31.712 --> 00:00:35.880
You set a discount like 5% off or $2 off, and

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:39.466
the customer clicks a little box to clip it before they buy.

00:00:39.466 --> 00:00:40.960
In the past, we've used

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:46.160
the promotional coupons for three main things, product launches, reviving slow sales, and

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:46.769
the holidays.

00:00:46.769 --> 00:00:51.640
For example, when we saw a random sales dip a few months ago, we didn't panic.

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:57.320
Instead, we turned on a simple $2 off coupon, and that promotion made us stand out amongst

00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:58.531
all the other listings.

00:00:58.531 --> 00:01:01.560
Our click-through rate jumped almost immediately, and our sales

00:01:01.963 --> 00:01:03.171
velocity eventually recovered.

00:01:03.171 --> 00:01:07.600
In short, coupons can catch the scroll and the eye of

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:11.548
the customer in a way a normal price tag just can't.

00:01:11.548 --> 00:01:12.983
Here's a pro tip.

00:01:12.983 --> 00:01:14.060
Know your psychology.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:18.785
If your item is under $20, use a percentage off promotion instead of a dollar amount.

00:01:18.785 --> 00:01:19.080
It

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:21.414
feels like a bigger deal to the customer.

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:24.040
If it's over $20, use a dollar amount, since

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:27.505
the customer will perceive that as real cash in their pocket.

00:01:27.505 --> 00:01:28.450
But be careful.

00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:29.080
You don't

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:34.760
want to stack discounts by accident, or you might end up selling your product for free.

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:37.680
Use coupons and promotions wisely and watch your sales grow.
